=== SIGNATURE ===
route_edges(board, start_ref, move_rule, [dirs], [max_steps])

=== COMMENT ===
Directed shortest paths. move_rule(from,to,dir) returns a nonnegative edge cost or NA()/text for an illegal move. Optional arrow string limits directions. Returns least cost to every cell; start is 0.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(board, start_ref, move_rule, [dirs], [max_steps],
  LET(
    row_count, ROWS(board),
    col_count, COLUMNS(board),
    infinity, 1E99,
    all_dirs, {"↑"; "↓"; "←"; "→"; "↖"; "↗"; "↙"; "↘"},
    dir_text, IF(ISOMITTED(dirs), "↑↓←→↖↗↙↘", dirs),
    dir_list, FILTER(all_dirs, ISNUMBER(SEARCH(all_dirs, dir_text))),
    step_count, MAX(1, INT(IF(ISOMITTED(max_steps), MAX(row_count, col_count) - 1, max_steps))),
    start_coords, IF(
      ROWS(start_ref) * COLUMNS(start_ref) = 1,
      LET(
        start_num, num_ad(start_ref),
        HSTACK(
          INT(start_num / 1000000) - MIN(ROW(board)) + 1,
          MOD(start_num, 1000000) - MIN(COLUMN(board)) + 1
        )
      ),
      start_ref
    ),
    start_row, INDEX(start_coords, 1),
    start_col, INDEX(start_coords, 2),
    initial_costs, MAKEARRAY(
      row_count,
      col_count,
      LAMBDA(row_ix, col_ix, IF(AND(row_ix = start_row, col_ix = start_col), 0, infinity))
    ),
    IF(
      OR(start_row < 1, start_row > row_count, start_col < 1, start_col > col_count),
      "X",
      LET(
        result, REDUCE(
          initial_costs,
          SEQUENCE(step_count),
          LAMBDA(costs, unused, z_route_edges_step(costs, board, move_rule, dir_list, infinity))
        ),
        checked, z_route_edges_step(result, board, move_rule, dir_list, infinity),
        IF(
          SUM(--(checked < result)) > 0,
          "MORE STEPS",
          IF(result >= infinity / 2, "", result)
        )
      )
    )
  )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Least-cost distance from a start cell to every reachable cell when move legality or cost can depend on direction and on both cells.

Arguments:
  board       - rectangular map or helper array. Cell values are passed to move_rule.
  start_ref   - starting cell as A1 text, a numeric address (1e6*row+col), or a {row, col} coordinate pair relative to board.
  move_rule   - LAMBDA(from_cell, to_cell, dir). Return a nonnegative move cost for a legal move; return NA(), text, or a negative value for an illegal move. Other Excel errors remain visible.
  [dirs]      - string of allowed arrow characters. Defaults to all eight directions: ↑↓←→↖↗↙↘.
  [max_steps] - maximum edges allowed in a route. Defaults to the larger board dimension minus one. If that is insufficient for a winding route, the function returns "MORE STEPS"; rerun with a larger value.

Returns:
  An array the same size as board containing the least cost from the start to every reachable cell. The start is 0. Unreachable cells are blank. An out-of-range start returns "X". If another relaxation can still improve a cost after max_steps, returns "MORE STEPS" instead of an incomplete distance map.

The solver uses synchronous Bellman-Ford-style relaxation through the private z_route_edges_step helper. It requires no circular references or iterative-calculation setting. The complete route state must be the current cell; rules involving previous direction, collected keys, or other path history require an expanded state.

Example:
  =LET(rule,LAMBDA(from_cell,to_cell,dir,XLOOKUP(dir,{"↑","↓","←","→","↖","↗","↙","↘"},{3,3,4,4,5,5,5,5},NA())),route_edges(A1:C3,"B2",rule,,8))
  returns the 3-4-5 directional distance map from B2.
